    "function": "Involved in base excision repair of DNA damaged by oxidation or by mutagenic agents. DNA glycosylase that recognizes and removes damaged pyrimidines. Excises Tg:A (thymine glycol, prefers 5R isomers), Tg:G, 5,6-dihydrouracil:G base pairs and urea:A, also excises oxidized purine derivatives guanidinohydantoin:C and spiroiminodihydantoin:C. Poorly cleaves dsDNA with uracil substitutions, thus also acting as a weak uracil-DNA glycosylase. Acts on DNA bubble and 3'-fork structures, suggesting a role in replication-associated DNA repair. Activity on 7,8-dihydro-8-oxoguanine (8-oxoG) is debated; a r",
